{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-41713","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74262","text":"Round 27, pass B3 — the native float plane: measured first, then asserted"}]},{"id":"blk-41714","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74263","marks":["bold"],"text":"Your sequence, taken exactly: C-side measurement as the first sub-pass of the substantive round, an independent C↔JS diff inspected before any conformance assertion, and continuation only because the relation actually agreed."}]},{"id":"blk-41715","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74264","text":"One correction on the packaging: this landed as "},{"id":"spn-74265","marks":["bold"],"text":"one commit, not two"},{"id":"spn-74266","text":". The two sub-passes were genuinely done and gated in order — B3.1's reducer, "},{"id":"spn-74267","marks":["code"],"text":"--measure"},{"id":"spn-74268","text":" mode and comparator were built, the whole gate was run green, and the 27-fixture diff was inspected, all before a line of B3.2's conformance assertions existed — but the B3.1 and B3.2 edits interleave inside four files ("},{"id":"spn-74269","marks":["code"],"text":"film_check.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74270","text":", "},{"id":"spn-74271","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74272","text":", "},{"id":"spn-74273","marks":["code"],"text":"negative_battery.sh"},{"id":"spn-74274","text":", "},{"id":"spn-74275","marks":["code"],"text":"invariant-grid.json"},{"id":"spn-74276","text":"), and a hunk-split would have produced a first commit I never actually ran. The ledger carries the two sub-passes separately (items 275–286 and 287–297) and that is the authoritative record of the order."}]},{"id":"blk-41716","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74277","text":"Gate: grid "},{"id":"spn-74278","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.41.0"},{"id":"spn-74279","text":" (88 entries / 379 citations) · "},{"id":"spn-74280","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge/ic32_film.c"},{"id":"spn-74281","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74282","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.3.0"},{"id":"spn-74283","text":" · negative battery "},{"id":"spn-74284","marks":["bold"],"text":"295/295"},{"id":"spn-74285","text":" · film "},{"id":"spn-74286","marks":["bold"],"text":"25/25"},{"id":"spn-74287","text":" · lowering "},{"id":"spn-74288","marks":["bold"],"text":"23/23"},{"id":"spn-74289","text":" · derive 45/45 · realm 24/24 · bridge "},{"id":"spn-74290","marks":["bold"],"text":"48/48"},{"id":"spn-74291","text":" · harness 9/9 · runner 3/3 · "},{"id":"spn-74292","marks":["bold"],"text":"measure-compare 27/27 (non-gating)"},{"id":"spn-74293","text":". "},{"id":"spn-74294","marks":["code"],"text":"cert_id a08ee15d…"},{"id":"spn-74295","text":" byte-identical — "},{"id":"spn-74296","marks":["bold"],"text":"thirty-sixth"},{"id":"spn-74297","text":" consecutive round."}]},{"id":"blk-41717","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74298","text":"1. The measurement came first, and it agreed on 27 fixtures rather than 1"}]},{"id":"blk-41718","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74299","text":"You asked for "},{"id":"spn-74300","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-74301","text":". I ran the whole conformance corpus plus the three film fixtures, because one fixture cannot tell you whether an instrument works — see §2, which is exactly that."}]},{"id":"blk-41719","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74302","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge/measure_compare.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74303","text":" runs the JS reference relation and "},{"id":"spn-74304","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32_film --measure"},{"id":"spn-74305","text":" and diffs:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41721","spans":[{"id":"spn-74306","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-41722","spans":[{"id":"spn-74307","text":"fields"}]}],"id":"blk-41720","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41723","spans":[{"id":"spn-74308","marks":["bold"],"text":"SEMANTIC"}]},{"id":"blk-41724","spans":[{"id":"spn-74309","text":"frame ordering · rule · plane · canonical locus · "},{"id":"spn-74310","marks":["code"],"text":"pre_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-74311","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-74312","marks":["code"],"text":"post_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-74313","text":" · terminal class · steps · "},{"id":"spn-74314","marks":["code"],"text":"final_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-74315","text":" · normal form · "},{"id":"spn-74316","marks":["code"],"text":"normal_form_id"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41725","spans":[{"id":"spn-74317","marks":["bold"],"text":"DIAGNOSTIC"}]},{"id":"blk-41726","spans":[{"id":"spn-74318","text":"the whole "},{"id":"spn-74319","marks":["bold"],"text":"enabled SET"},{"id":"spn-74320","text":" per frame · rule tally · locus-family tally · signature length"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41727","spans":[{"id":"spn-74321","marks":["bold"],"text":"NOT COMPARED, said out loud"}]},{"id":"blk-41728","spans":[{"id":"spn-74322","text":"ic32's "},{"id":"spn-74323","marks":["code"],"text":"interactions"},{"id":"spn-74324","text":" — not plane-classified, so it is a different quantity from the kernel's INTERACT-plane readback claim. Both printed."}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41729","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74325","marks":["bold"],"text":"27/27 agree."},{"id":"spn-74326","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74327","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-74328","text":" is 21 frames — "},{"id":"spn-74329","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-LAM 6 · DUP-SUP= 4 · DUP-LAM 3 · DUP-VAR 3 · APP-SUP 2 · DUP-APP 2 · DUP-SUP! 1"},{"id":"spn-74330","text":", "},{"id":"spn-74331","marks":["code"],"text":"t: 4 · d: 13 · v: 4"},{"id":"spn-74332","text":", NORMAL_FORM at "},{"id":"spn-74333","marks":["code"],"text":"λa.(S (S (S (S a))))"},{"id":"spn-74334","text":". "},{"id":"spn-74335","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_3_3"},{"id":"spn-74336","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-74337","marks":["bold"],"text":"91 frames with 87 dup-plane loci"},{"id":"spn-74338","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41730","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74339","marks":["bold"],"text":"Your `enabled_count` ruling, and one step past it."},{"id":"spn-74340","text":" It stays out of the film. But the comparator now diffs the whole enabled "},{"id":"spn-74341","marks":["bold"],"text":"SET"},{"id":"spn-74342","text":" rather than its cardinality — two enumerations can agree on every chosen redex and every state across a whole corpus and still disagree about what else was available, and that divergence stays invisible until the day the strategy changes. Diagnostic, in a tool that commits nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-41731","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74343","marks":["bold"],"text":"No expected table exists in the emitter or the comparator."},{"id":"spn-74344","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74345","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-74346","text":" now refuses the fixture term in either file. The fixture belongs in the check; an expected answer for it inside the emitter is how a conformance theorem becomes a transcription theorem, and nothing downstream could tell."}]},{"id":"blk-41732","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74347","text":"2. The comparator's first find was a defect in the comparator"}]},{"id":"blk-41733","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74348","text":"It reported "},{"id":"spn-74349","marks":["code"],"text":"lowered_add_2_3"},{"id":"spn-74350","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74351","marks":["bold"],"text":"DIFFER"},{"id":"spn-74352","text":" on "},{"id":"spn-74353","marks":["code"],"text":"terminal final"},{"id":"spn-74354","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-74355","marks":["code"],"text":"signature length"},{"id":"spn-74356","text":" (JS 40 vs C 65 — the "},{"id":"spn-74357","marks":["code"],"text":"#"},{"id":"spn-74358","text":"-prefixed §5 compaction marker) while "},{"id":"spn-74359","marks":["bold"],"text":"all six frames matched exactly"},{"id":"spn-74360","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41734","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74361","text":"The C computes its final signature before calling "},{"id":"spn-74362","marks":["code"],"text":"normal()"},{"id":"spn-74363","text":". My JS side read "},{"id":"spn-74364","marks":["code"],"text":"semStateId"},{"id":"spn-74365","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-74366","marks":["code"],"text":"semStateSignature"},{"id":"spn-74367","text":" inside an object literal evaluated "},{"id":"spn-74368","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-74369","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74370","marks":["code"],"text":"readback"},{"id":"spn-74371","text":", which folds the live heap and "},{"id":"spn-74372","marks":["bold"],"text":"fires rules into the same runtime"},{"id":"spn-74373","text":". It was measuring a state the film never reached."}]},{"id":"blk-41735","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74374","marks":["bold"],"text":"`church_exp_2_2` hid it"},{"id":"spn-74375","text":", because there the readback fires nothing at all ("},{"id":"spn-74376","marks":["code"],"text":"interactFired 0 · collapseFired 0 · liveCount 0"},{"id":"spn-74377","text":") and the two reads coincide. A fixture on which an instrument's bug is invisible is not a fixture that validates the instrument."}]},{"id":"blk-41736","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74378","text":"3. Agreement is worth nothing until the comparator has been shown to differ"}]},{"id":"blk-41737","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74379","text":"Three perturbed C builds, none committed:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41739","spans":[{"id":"spn-74380","text":"perturbation"}]},{"id":"blk-41740","spans":[{"id":"spn-74381","text":"fixtures that DIFFER"}]}],"id":"blk-41738","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41741","spans":[{"id":"spn-74382","text":"enumeration order R2L → L2R"}]},{"id":"blk-41742","spans":[{"id":"spn-74383","text":"8"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41743","spans":[{"id":"spn-74384","text":"locus index order L2R → R2L"}]},{"id":"blk-41744","spans":[{"id":"spn-74385","text":"12"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41745","spans":[{"id":"spn-74386","text":"child push order in the app walk not reversed"}]},{"id":"blk-41746","spans":[{"id":"spn-74387","text":"2"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41747","spans":[{"id":"spn-74388","marks":["italic"],"text":"(added later, for the enabled-SET field)"},{"id":"spn-74389","text":" dup-value redexes reordered"}]},{"id":"blk-41748","spans":[{"id":"spn-74390","text":"10"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41749","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74391","text":"The locus-order one reports "},{"id":"spn-74392","marks":["code"],"text":"frame 3 locus: JS d:0 vs C d:1"},{"id":"spn-74393","text":" on "},{"id":"spn-74394","marks":["code"],"text":"church_apply_3"},{"id":"spn-74395","text":" — a real dup, correctly enumerated, "},{"id":"spn-74396","marks":["bold"],"text":"named by the wrong index"},{"id":"spn-74397","text":". Precisely the failure you told the round to be strict about, and precisely the one a count-only diagnostic cannot see."}]},{"id":"blk-41750","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74398","text":"4. The thing you warned about is real: they are two different traversals"}]},{"id":"blk-41751","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74399","text":"You wrote "},{"id":"spn-74400","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"don't let C implement something equivalent enough and then translate the locus afterward.\""},{"id":"spn-74401","text":" The kernel does not have one live-cell order, it has "},{"id":"spn-74402","marks":["bold"],"text":"two"},{"id":"spn-74403","text":", and they disagree:"}]},{"id":"blk-41752","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41754","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74404","marks":["bold"],"text":"`liveHeap`"},{"id":"spn-74405","text":" pushes children FORWARD → pops "},{"id":"spn-74406","marks":["bold"],"text":"right-to-left"},{"id":"spn-74407","text":". This orders the ENUMERATION, so it"}]}],"id":"blk-41753","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41755","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74408","text":"decides which redex is leftmost."}]},{"id":"blk-41756","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41758","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74409","marks":["bold"],"text":"`liveDiscoveryOrder`"},{"id":"spn-74410","text":" pushes children REVERSED → pops "},{"id":"spn-74411","marks":["bold"],"text":"left-to-right"},{"id":"spn-74412","text":". This indexes the"}]}],"id":"blk-41757","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41759","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74413","marks":["code"],"text":"d:"},{"id":"spn-74414","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-74415","marks":["code"],"text":"v:"},{"id":"spn-74416","text":" loci, so it decides what NUMBER the chosen redex's locus carries."}]},{"id":"blk-41760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74417","text":"Collapsing either onto the other still produces a locus that names a real, live, correctly-enumerated redex — just not the one that fired. "},{"id":"spn-74418","marks":["code"],"text":"live_cells(root, direction)"},{"id":"spn-74419","text":" implements both and every caller says which it wants. The law records it and a forgery holds it there."}]},{"id":"blk-41761","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74420","text":"5. ic32 cannot substitute a dup by name — and that cost is representational, not semantic"}]},{"id":"blk-41762","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74421","marks":["code"],"text":"FloatRt"},{"id":"spn-74422","text":" keeps dups in a side table with the projections as NAMES, so firing one is two substitutions and the occurrence never has to be found. ic32 has no such table: "},{"id":"spn-74423","marks":["code"],"text":"heap[D]"},{"id":"spn-74424","text":" is the cell's "},{"id":"spn-74425","marks":["bold"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-74426","text":" before the rule fires and the "},{"id":"spn-74427","marks":["bold"],"text":"other side's substitution"},{"id":"spn-74428","text":" afterwards. So a dup can only be fired "},{"id":"spn-74429","marks":["bold"],"text":"from a demanded side"},{"id":"spn-74430","text":", and the demanded projection must be replaced where it stands."}]},{"id":"blk-41763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74431","marks":["code"],"text":"find_projections"},{"id":"spn-74432","text":" walks every reachable slot — structural children, substitution slots (an APP-LAM whose argument was a projection writes it into the binder's slot), and live cell values — and "},{"id":"spn-74433","marks":["bold"],"text":"refuses (`film-projection-not-unique`) rather than choosing"},{"id":"spn-74434","text":" if a projection is not unique. A linear net has exactly one; \"exactly one\" is a property to check, not a fact to rely on."}]},{"id":"blk-41764","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74435","text":"The rules fired are "},{"id":"spn-74436","marks":["bold"],"text":"ic32's own `fire()` and `app_sup()`, unedited"},{"id":"spn-74437","text":". The rules are the runtime's; the scheduling and the addressing are the film's."}]},{"id":"blk-41765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74438","marks":["bold"],"text":"One thing I want your read on"},{"id":"spn-74439","text":" — §9(b)."}]},{"id":"blk-41766","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74440","text":"6. The conformance claim — "},{"id":"spn-74441","marks":["code"],"text":"film.native-emission@2"}]},{"id":"blk-41767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74442","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-74443","text":" emits "},{"id":"spn-74444","marks":["bold"],"text":"21 chained native frames"},{"id":"spn-74445","text":" covering "},{"id":"spn-74446","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-LAM · APP-SUP · DUP-LAM · DUP-SUP= · DUP-SUP! · DUP-VAR · DUP-APP"},{"id":"spn-74447","text":" across "},{"id":"spn-74448","marks":["bold"],"text":"`t:`, `d:`, `v:`"},{"id":"spn-74449","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-74450","marks":["bold"],"text":"both semantic planes"},{"id":"spn-74451","text":", and the kernel's own "},{"id":"spn-74452","marks":["code"],"text":"replaySemFilm"},{"id":"spn-74453","text":" accepts the whole chain on "},{"id":"spn-74454","marks":["code"],"text":"FloatRt"},{"id":"spn-74455","text":" and on "},{"id":"spn-74456","marks":["code"],"text":"DescFloatRt"},{"id":"spn-74457","text":". Endpoints are the corpus vector's own initial state and normal form, already agreed byte-for-byte by the 48/48 bridge — so the new claim is exactly the "},{"id":"spn-74458","marks":["bold"],"text":"21 transitions between them"},{"id":"spn-74459","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41768","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74460","text":"The coverage assertion is "},{"id":"spn-74461","marks":["bold"],"text":"derived from the film"},{"id":"spn-74462","text":" (which rules occur, which locus families, which planes); every forgery index is "},{"id":"spn-74463","marks":["bold"],"text":"found"},{"id":"spn-74464","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-74465","marks":["code"],"text":"firstFrame(f => …)"},{"id":"spn-74466","text":", never "},{"id":"spn-74467","marks":["code"],"text":"frames[6]"},{"id":"spn-74468","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-41769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74469","marks":["code"],"text":"@1"},{"id":"spn-74470","text":" is kept as "},{"id":"spn-74471","marks":["bold"],"text":"history, not withdrawn"},{"id":"spn-74472","text":" — it is not wrong about anything it claims, it is narrower, and it carries the two scope corrections "},{"id":"spn-74473","marks":["code"],"text":"@2"},{"id":"spn-74474","text":" does not repeat."}]},{"id":"blk-41770","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74475","marks":["bold"],"text":"ERA is enumerated and refuses."},{"id":"spn-74476","text":" Both, by name ("},{"id":"spn-74477","marks":["code"],"text":"film-era-rule-not-implemented"},{"id":"spn-74478","text":"). Enumeration must include them or \"no enabled work\" silently means \"no work of the kinds I implement\". Firing them without a witness would be coverage by hope. "},{"id":"spn-74479","marks":["bold"],"text":"`BUDGET_EXHAUSTED` is a typed refusal (`film-budget-exhausted`), never a terminal"},{"id":"spn-74480","text":", and the terminal is concluded only after a "},{"id":"spn-74481","marks":["bold"],"text":"fresh full-pool enumeration"},{"id":"spn-74482","text":" returns empty."}]},{"id":"blk-41771","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74483","text":"7. Seven forgeries on the new surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-41772","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74484","text":"A mid-chain edit needs every later frame's "},{"id":"spn-74485","marks":["code"],"text":"prev"},{"id":"spn-74486","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-74487","marks":["code"],"text":"frame_id"},{"id":"spn-74488","text":" rebuilt, so the round added a multi-frame "},{"id":"spn-74489","marks":["code"],"text":"rechain"},{"id":"spn-74490","text":"; the single-frame "},{"id":"spn-74491","marks":["code"],"text":"recommit"},{"id":"spn-74492","text":" could not express any of these."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41774","spans":[{"id":"spn-74493","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-41775","spans":[{"id":"spn-74494","text":"forgery"}]},{"id":"blk-41776","spans":[{"id":"spn-74495","text":"refusal"}]}],"id":"blk-41773","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41777","spans":[{"id":"spn-74496","text":"D-1"}]},{"id":"blk-41778","spans":[{"id":"spn-74497","text":"a "},{"id":"spn-74498","marks":["code"],"text":"d:"},{"id":"spn-74499","text":" index no live cell carries"}]},{"id":"blk-41779","spans":[{"id":"spn-74500","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-locus-not-enabled"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41780","spans":[{"id":"spn-74501","text":"D-2"}]},{"id":"blk-41781","spans":[{"id":"spn-74502","text":"a "},{"id":"spn-74503","marks":["code"],"text":"v:"},{"id":"spn-74504","text":" path extended past any application"}]},{"id":"blk-41782","spans":[{"id":"spn-74505","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-locus-not-enabled"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41783","spans":[{"id":"spn-74506","text":"D-3"}]},{"id":"blk-41784","spans":[{"id":"spn-74507","marks":["code"],"text":"DUP-SUP="},{"id":"spn-74508","text":" relabelled as its sibling "},{"id":"spn-74509","marks":["code"],"text":"DUP-SUP!"}]},{"id":"blk-41785","spans":[{"id":"spn-74510","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-rule-mismatch"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41786","spans":[{"id":"spn-74511","text":"D-4"}]},{"id":"blk-41787","spans":[{"id":"spn-74512","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-SUP"},{"id":"spn-74513","text":" relabelled "},{"id":"spn-74514","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-LAM"}]},{"id":"blk-41788","spans":[{"id":"spn-74515","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-rule-mismatch"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41789","spans":[{"id":"spn-74516","text":"D-5"}]},{"id":"blk-41790","spans":[{"id":"spn-74517","text":"a COLLAPSE frame claiming INTERACT"}]},{"id":"blk-41791","spans":[{"id":"spn-74518","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-plane-mismatch"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41792","spans":[{"id":"spn-74519","text":"D-6"}]},{"id":"blk-41793","spans":[{"id":"spn-74520","text":"the honest film stopped one frame early, terminal HONESTLY recomputed"}]},{"id":"blk-41794","spans":[{"id":"spn-74521","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-false-normal-form"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41795","spans":[{"id":"spn-74522","text":"D-7"}]},{"id":"blk-41796","spans":[{"id":"spn-74523","text":"a locus naming a "},{"id":"spn-74524","marks":["bold"],"text":"different redex that really is live and enabled"}]},{"id":"blk-41797","spans":[{"id":"spn-74525","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-post-mismatch"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41798","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74526","marks":["bold"],"text":"D-5 is only possible now."},{"id":"spn-74527","text":" Every native frame before this round was INTERACT, so the "},{"id":"spn-74528","marks":["code"],"text":"plane"},{"id":"spn-74529","text":" field had nothing else it could say. A hybrid-plane film is the first one in which "},{"id":"spn-74530","marks":["code"],"text":"law:plane.rule-partition@1"},{"id":"spn-74531","text":" is forgeable at all."}]},{"id":"blk-41799","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74532","marks":["bold"],"text":"D-6 is your terminal point, manufactured against the fixture that carried the disease."},{"id":"spn-74533","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74534","marks":["code"],"text":"l_prog_history.round_4_diagnosis"},{"id":"spn-74535","text":" names "},{"id":"spn-74536","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-74537","text":" at step 15 as the false-quiescence witness that falsified "},{"id":"spn-74538","marks":["code"],"text":"law:sched.free.ast-term@1"},{"id":"spn-74539","text":". D-6 stops one frame early and recomputes "},{"id":"spn-74540","marks":["code"],"text":"steps"},{"id":"spn-74541","text":", "},{"id":"spn-74542","marks":["code"],"text":"last_frame"},{"id":"spn-74543","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-74544","marks":["code"],"text":"final_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-74545","text":" for the state it really stops in, so "},{"id":"spn-74546","marks":["bold"],"text":"every bookkeeping check passes"},{"id":"spn-74547","text":"; replay refuses it because it re-enumerates the pool at the terminal and finds work."}]},{"id":"blk-41800","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74548","marks":["bold"],"text":"D-7 is the only one that distinguishes \"the locus names A redex\" from \"the locus names THE redex.\""},{"id":"spn-74549","text":" It replays the film's first "},{"id":"spn-74550","marks":["italic"],"text":"k"},{"id":"spn-74551","text":" frames with the kernel's own machinery, enumerates the live redexes, and picks one with the SAME rule at a DIFFERENT locus — frame 4 fired "},{"id":"spn-74552","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-LAM"},{"id":"spn-74553","text":" at "},{"id":"spn-74554","marks":["code"],"text":"t:"},{"id":"spn-74555","text":" while "},{"id":"spn-74556","marks":["code"],"text":"t:arg"},{"id":"spn-74557","text":" was equally live and equally "},{"id":"spn-74558","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-LAM"},{"id":"spn-74559","text":". It gets past enabledness entirely and dies on the post-state. If a fixture ever has no such alternative the case "},{"id":"spn-74560","marks":["bold"],"text":"reports it could not be built"},{"id":"spn-74561","text":" rather than skipping."}]},{"id":"blk-41801","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74562","text":"8. Three stale records, and one forgery that had retired itself"}]},{"id":"blk-41802","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74563","marks":["bold"],"text":"Two ratchets."},{"id":"spn-74564","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74565","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-74566","text":" required the literal "},{"id":"spn-74567","marks":["code"],"text":"film-dup-rule-enabled"},{"id":"spn-74568","text":" in the emitter, and"}]}],"id":"blk-41803","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41805","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74569","marks":["code"],"text":"film_check"},{"id":"spn-74570","text":" asserted a DUP-SUP term is refused. Both were true at v0.2.0 and "},{"id":"spn-74571","marks":["bold"],"text":"both would have blocked the round that closed the gap"},{"id":"spn-74572","text":" — the species B1.2.1 named. "},{"id":"spn-74573","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering_check"},{"id":"spn-74574","text":"'s \"STILL NOT CLAIMED\" list is now "},{"id":"spn-74575","marks":["bold"],"text":"PROBED"},{"id":"spn-74576","text":" from the emitter rather than typed."}]},{"id":"blk-41806","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74577","marks":["bold"],"text":"A refinement grade that would have improved for free."},{"id":"spn-74578","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74579","marks":["code"],"text":"derivation.lowering-refinement@4"},{"id":"spn-74580","text":" said"}]}],"id":"blk-41807","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41809","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74581","text":"the open item was \"a fixture where a DUP-* rule actually becomes enabled\". Closed — "},{"id":"spn-74582","marks":["bold"],"text":"by `church_exp_2_2` under `film.native-emission@2`, and NOT by the refinement fixture"},{"id":"spn-74583","text":", which still fires no dup rule and still emits the same six APP-LAM frames. Both records now say so. At v0.2.0 those six frames were the emitter's LIMIT; at v0.3.0 they are a fact about the TERM."}]},{"id":"blk-41810","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41812","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74584","marks":["bold"],"text":"A forgery keyed on a version literal."},{"id":"spn-74585","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74586","marks":["code"],"text":"film-emitter-version-drifts"},{"id":"spn-74587","text":" forged"}]}],"id":"blk-41811","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41813","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74588","marks":["code"],"text":"emitter_version\":\"0.2.0"},{"id":"spn-74589","text":"; the bump made it a no-op and the non-vacuity detector said so on the first run. Regex now. "},{"id":"spn-74590","marks":["bold"],"text":"Third time"},{"id":"spn-74591","text":" a version literal inside a forgery has retired itself silently."}]},{"id":"blk-41814","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74592","marks":["bold"],"text":"A property re-homed rather than dropped."},{"id":"spn-74593","text":" The grid assertion for the removed"}]}],"id":"blk-41815","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41817","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74594","text":"readback-interaction-count record now reads "},{"id":"spn-74595","marks":["code"],"text":"@1"},{"id":"spn-74596","text":", where that v0.1.0 fact lives, and independently the C source still carries it and is still checked. Deleting an assertion because a revision bump moved its subject is how a property is lost in a rename."}]},{"id":"blk-41818","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74597","text":"9. Three things for you"}]},{"id":"blk-41819","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74598","marks":["bold"],"text":"(a) The catalog family id is `impl-c-ic32-film-v0.1.0` and the binary is v0.3.0."},{"id":"spn-74599","text":" Nothing is wrong today — artifact identity is the DIGEST, which does move, and the family is a catalog key. But a version inside a name that nothing checks is the shape that drifts, and this round already caught one forgery that retired itself on a version literal. Options: drop the version from the family name; bump it and accept that every emitter bump is a catalog change; or leave it and record why. "},{"id":"spn-74600","marks":["bold"],"text":"Flagged, not changed"},{"id":"spn-74601","text":" — it touches a frozen probe's era wording and the observation keys, so it is a ruling."}]},{"id":"blk-41820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74602","marks":["bold"],"text":"(b) The one-interaction check is post-hoc."},{"id":"spn-74603","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74604","marks":["code"],"text":"fire(D,L,k)"},{"id":"spn-74605","text":" opens with "},{"id":"spn-74606","marks":["code"],"text":"whnf(heap[D])"},{"id":"spn-74607","text":", which could in principle do work. I argue it cannot here: "},{"id":"spn-74608","marks":["code"],"text":"dup_rule_name"},{"id":"spn-74609","text":" has already established by "},{"id":"spn-74610","marks":["bold"],"text":"chasing"},{"id":"spn-74611","text":" that the value is a Lam/Sup/Era/free-Var/stuck-App, and "},{"id":"spn-74612","marks":["code"],"text":"whnf"},{"id":"spn-74613","text":" returns each of those without an interaction. The emitter then checks "},{"id":"spn-74614","marks":["code"],"text":"interactions - before == 1"},{"id":"spn-74615","text":" — but that check runs "},{"id":"spn-74616","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-74617","text":" the mutation, so a violated precondition is caught rather than prevented. Is a post-hoc counter check the right instrument here, or should the emitter assert the precondition structurally before calling in?"}]},{"id":"blk-41821","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74618","marks":["bold"],"text":"(c) The `v:` locus and shared subterms."},{"id":"spn-74619","text":" Each "},{"id":"spn-74620","marks":["code"],"text":"findAppRedexes"},{"id":"spn-74621","text":" call carries its own visited set, so a node reachable both from the root and from inside a dup value is enumerated "},{"id":"spn-74622","marks":["bold"],"text":"twice"},{"id":"spn-74623","text":", under a "},{"id":"spn-74624","marks":["code"],"text":"t:"},{"id":"spn-74625","text":" locus and a "},{"id":"spn-74626","marks":["code"],"text":"v:"},{"id":"spn-74627","text":" locus. C reproduces that faithfully and the corpus agrees. I have not found a fixture where the two loci name the same redex and a film could legitimately cite either — is that worth a purpose-built witness, or is it a non-question because both loci fire the same rule to the same post-state?"}]},{"id":"blk-41822","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74628","text":"10. Next, in your order"}]},{"id":"blk-41823","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41825","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74629","marks":["bold"],"text":"The ERA witnesses"},{"id":"spn-74630","text":" — two fixtures, not one contrived term containing both: coverage by"}]}],"id":"blk-41824","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-41826","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74631","text":"construction. Both "},{"id":"spn-74632","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-ERA"},{"id":"spn-74633","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-74634","marks":["code"],"text":"DUP-ERA"},{"id":"spn-74635","text":", since the measurement showed neither fires here."}]},{"id":"blk-41827","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41829","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74636","marks":["bold"],"text":"BUDGET_EXHAUSTED"},{"id":"spn-74637","text":" native film evidence, currently a typed refusal."}]}],"id":"blk-41828","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74638","marks":["bold"],"text":"`EMISSION_CONFORMANCE-v1`"},{"id":"spn-74639","text":" over "},{"id":"spn-74640","marks":["code"],"text":"{closed_template → target_term_sem_id}"},{"id":"spn-74641","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-41830","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-41832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74642","text":"C-side replay — films flowing the other direction — remains unclaimed and unchanged."}]},{"id":"blk-41833","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74643","text":"Files"}]},{"id":"blk-41834","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41836","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74644","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_B3_REVIEW_PACK.tar.gz"},{"id":"spn-74645","text":" — runs from any extraction dir; "},{"id":"spn-74646","marks":["code"],"text":"./verify.sh"},{"id":"spn-74647","text":" replays every gate "},{"id":"spn-74648","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"}]}],"id":"blk-41835","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74649","text":"the non-gating measurement, and writes "},{"id":"spn-74650","marks":["code"],"text":"RESULTS.txt"},{"id":"spn-74651","text":" from the run."}]},{"id":"blk-41838","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41840","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74652","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/round-11-ledger.md"},{"id":"spn-74653","text":" §§ B3.1 (items 275–286) and B3.2 (items 287–297)."}]}],"id":"blk-41839","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74654","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/bridge/ic32_film.c"},{"id":"spn-74655","text":" v0.3.0 · "},{"id":"spn-74656","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/bridge/measure_compare.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74657","text":" ·"}]}],"id":"blk-41841","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74658","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/bridge/film_check.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74659","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41844","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41846","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74660","text":"Reproduce the measurement: "},{"id":"spn-74661","marks":["code"],"text":"make gov-measure"},{"id":"spn-74662","text":" (not in "},{"id":"spn-74663","marks":["code"],"text":"make governance"},{"id":"spn-74664","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-41845","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierawrkpmxqxwfq2s25zwv77hoiahn5ecrpv45zmjw2vduz62ppcrvba","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}